theorem two-numeral-facts-joined-by-and
  note        "A. B." and "A and B" are one claim (SYNTAX.md), and
              arithmetic works out each part.
  then 2·3 = 6 and 1 < 2

1.  2·3 = 6 and 1 < 2
    arithmetic

theorem two-real-facts-joined-by-and
  then √4 = 2 and π > 3

1.  √4 = 2 and π > 3
    real arithmetic
